#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# integer_string

#% text
# `integer_string(n)` gives the decimal digits of `abs(n)` as a string; `integer_string(n, b)` uses base `b`; `integer_string(n, b, len)` has exactly `len` characters.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Digits above 9 are the letters `a` to `z`, so the base is at most 36.

#% item
# A shorter result is padded with zeros on the left, a longer one cut to its last `len` characters.

#% item
# `integer_string(n, "Roman")` gives a Roman numeral for 0 < n < 4000.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
integer_string(1988, "Roman")
#% output
#= "MCMLXXXVIII"

#% cell
integer_string(255, 16)
#% output
#= "ff"

#% cell
integer_string(5, 2, 8)
#% output
#= "00000101"

#% cell
integer_string(12345, 10, 3)
#% output
#= "345"

#% cell
integer_string(-42)
#% output
#= "42"

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_digits`, `from_digits`, `to_string`
